
Interfacce di as10r1:

  1) eth0  LAN A     192.168.0.1/30
  2) eth1  LAN L     110.0.0.1/24

Interfaccia di cui cambiare l'IP (numero, Invio = annulla): 1

as10r1 eth0 (LAN A): IP attuale 192.168.0.1/30
Sulla LAN A (192.168.0.0/30) ci sono anche: as40r1 192.168.0.2/30
Nuovo IP (es. 192.168.0.1/30; senza maschera tiene /30; Invio = annulla): 192.168.50.1/30
⚠️ 192.168.50.1/30 non è nella rete della LAN A (192.168.0.0/30): gli altri dispositivi della LAN non lo raggiungerebbero.
  1) cambia la rete di tutta la LAN (anche gli IP degli altri)
  2) cambia solo questo IP
  0) annulla
Scelta: 1

LAN A: rete 192.168.0.0/30; as10r1 eth0 192.168.0.1/30, as40r1 eth0 192.168.0.2/30

LAN A: 192.168.0.0/30 -> 192.168.50.0/30
   as10r1     eth0  192.168.0.1/30 -> 192.168.50.1/30
   as40r1     eth0  192.168.0.2/30 -> 192.168.50.2/30

--- Rete della LAN A: 192.168.0.0/30 -> 192.168.50.0/30: anteprima (4 file) ---
  as10r1.startup
    - riga   1: ip address add 192.168.0.1/30 dev eth0
    + riga   1: ip address add 192.168.50.1/30 dev eth0
  as10r1/etc/frr/frr.conf
    - riga  15: network 192.168.0.0/30
    + riga  15: network 192.168.50.0/30
    - riga  18: neighbor 192.168.0.2 remote-as 40
    - riga  19: neighbor 192.168.0.2 description Router as40r1
    + riga  18: neighbor 192.168.50.2 remote-as 40
    + riga  19: neighbor 192.168.50.2 description Router as40r1
    - riga  21: neighbor 192.168.0.2 prefix-list PL_as10r1_192_168_0_2_in in
    + riga  21: neighbor 192.168.50.2 prefix-list PL_as10r1_192_168_0_2_in in
  as40r1.startup
    - riga   1: ip address add 192.168.0.2/30 dev eth0
    + riga   1: ip address add 192.168.50.2/30 dev eth0
  as40r1/etc/frr/frr.conf
    - riga  15: network 192.168.0.0/30
    + riga  15: network 192.168.50.0/30
    - riga  20: neighbor 192.168.0.1 remote-as 10
    - riga  21: neighbor 192.168.0.1 description Router as10r1
    + riga  20: neighbor 192.168.50.1 remote-as 10
    + riga  21: neighbor 192.168.50.1 description Router as10r1

